🎯 Project Objective
The core objective of this laboratory repository is to design, implement, and validate foundational software modules using **Java 21**, **Apache Maven**, and **JUnit 5 (Jupiter)**. The workspace applies rigorous test-driven principles to assess operational correctness, handle exceptional state bounds, prevent regression issues, and document critical code execution pathways via readable automated assertions.

📦 Implemented Packages & Completed Tasks

🏁 Core System Configuration & Task Layout
All logical files are mapped and dynamically executed inside a single, unified Maven project space without dependencies clashing or cross-compilation failures. 

The workspace cleanly splits responsibilities across two active packages:

1. `BankAccount` Package (Homework Deliverables)
    Homework 1 – Core System Base: Formulated the underlying arithmetic calculation framework using `CalculatorApp.java` and verified operations via `CalculatorAppTest.java`.
    Homework 2 – Account Validation: Engineered banking logic handling validation constraints. Disallows negative values and monitors state balances under `$100` via `BankAccount1.java` and `BankAccount1Test.java`.
    Homework 3 – String Utility Testing: Developed advanced text-processing rules. Includes structural palindrome algorithms, vowel tallies, and multi-word anagram array matching inside `StringAnalyzer.java`. Validated execution using explicit JUnit 5 `@DisplayName` metrics in `StringAnalyzerTest.java`.

2. `ThirdLabTasks` Package (Lab Session Tasks)
    Lab Task 1 – Temperature Converter: Implemented precision-mapped thermodynamic conversion methods across Celsius, Fahrenheit, and Kelvin scales inside `TemperatureConverter.java` using exact delta assertions.
    Lab Task 2 – Bank Account Operations: Configured strict structural account boundaries within `LabBankAccount.java`. Validates that negative inputs trigger `IllegalArgumentException` and overdraft actions flag `IllegalStateException`.
    Lab Task 3 – Palindrome Checker String Utility: Programmed automated character cleaning pipelines inside `StringUtil.java` to screen alphanumeric characters and ignore letter case scales.
    Lab Task 4 – Simple Timer Utility: Managed elapsed time calculations within `TimerUtil.java` while checking chronological order bounds.
    Lab Task 5 – Shopping Cart Mini Case Study: Engineered memory-safe, array-backed transaction logic inside `ShoppingCart.java` to fulfill item additions, sequence deletions, missing item handling, and cart resets.
